# Agent PR workflow (Teqo)

**This repo overrides any user-level rule that says "always create PRs as draft".** Agent deliveries merge to `stage`, not `main`.

## Create (Ready, base stage)

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base stage --title "<id> — <title>" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## O que é
<2–4 linhas>

Closes #<N>
EOF
)"
```

- **Never** `--draft`. PRs must be **Ready for review** on creation.
- Base is always **`stage`** (never `main` — promote is human-only via `pnpm agent:promote --i-am-human`).

## Auto-merge immediately

Right after `gh pr create`, enable auto-merge:

```bash
gh pr merge --auto --merge
```

Do not wait for human approval. Auto-merge fires when **required** checks pass.

## Required checks vs Vercel

Branch protection on `stage` requires only:

- `checks` (GitHub Actions rollup from `ci-pr.yml`)
- `migration-lock`

**Vercel preview is NOT a merge gate.** Do not block on it.

When watching CI:

```bash
gh pr checks <PR> --watch --required
```

Use `--required` — without it, `--watch` also waits for Vercel and can stall for minutes on the Hobby plan (one concurrent build).

Once `checks` and `migration-lock` are green, auto-merge proceeds even if Vercel is still `PENDING`.

## Agent branches skip Vercel builds

Branches `agent/*` and `cursor/*` use `scripts/vercel-ignore-build.sh` so parallel agents do not queue Vercel builds. Previews still deploy for `stage` and `main`.

## Promote (human only)

Never run `gh pr create --base main` or `pnpm agent:promote` in the agent flow.
